Chapter: Recursive Eq

Section: Definitions

  Nest =
    | Leaf
    | Wrap (Nest)

  Chain =
    | End
    | Link (Integer) (Chain)

Section: Entry

 Chain carries a payload beside the recursive field, so a helper that
 compared only the recursive field would still answer eq for the two
 chains that differ at their last link.

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line (if Wrap Leaf == Wrap Leaf then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line (if Wrap (Wrap Leaf) == Wrap (Wrap Leaf) then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line (if Leaf == Leaf then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line (if Wrap Leaf == Leaf then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line (if Wrap (Wrap Leaf) == Wrap Leaf then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line (if Wrap Leaf /= Wrap Leaf then "ne" else "eq")
    print-line (if Wrap Leaf /= Leaf then "ne" else "eq")
    print-line (if Link 1 (Link 2 End) == Link 1 (Link 2 End) then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line (if Link 1 (Link 2 End) == Link 1 (Link 3 End) then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line (if Link 1 (Link 2 End) == Link 1 End then "eq" else "ne")
    print-line (if End == End then "eq" else "ne")
  end

